Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:24:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] iphlpapi: DHCP lease, interface state, forwarding, TTL, TCP
 and proxy-ARP changes through sg-netctl

Eleven calls that used to be FIXME stubs (several answering success without doing
anything) now act, the way Windows gates them: administrators only
(ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED), arguments validated first as Windows does, and routed to
sg-netctl, the network's one writer on this system.

  IpReleaseAddress / IpRenewAddress   release|renew DEVICE (DHCP lease of the index)
  SetIfEntry                          enable|disable DEVICE (admin status up/down;
                                      testing is ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED)
  EnableRouter / UnenableRouter       forwarding on|off, reference counted per
                                      OVERLAPPED, the pending request completes on
                                      Unenable; count returned
  SetIpStatistics / SetIpTTL          forwarding, ttl N (1..255)
  SetTcpEntry                         tcp delete LADDR LPORT RADDR RPORT; the connection
                                      must exist (ERROR_MR_MID_NOT_FOUND), the state must
                                      be DELETE_TCB, a non-administrator gets
                                      ERROR_NETWORK_ACCESS_DENIED (the conformance test's
                                      reading); three todo_wine marks in the iphlpapi
                                      test now pass and are removed
  CreateProxyArpEntry / DeleteProxyArpEntry   proxyarp add|del DEVICE ADDRESS MASK
  SetPerTcpConnectionEStats           validated and admin-checked, then ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED
                                      (this stack keeps no extended statistics)

With no sg-netctl, or one that does not know a request, the calls say
ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED. Gate: test/fastiphlp-gate.sh with a stand-in sg-netctl
(never the host's network).
